+## Context
+
+The repo has no `src/` yet; the package is ESM TypeScript with `node --test` and no dependencies.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+- Goals: strict RFC 6901 evaluation; a reusable building block for later features.
+- Non-Goals: URI fragment form, mutation, `-` (end-of-array) handling for writes.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Implement in `src/pointer.ts`, re-exported from `src/index.ts`. Plain `Error` subclass `JsonPointerError` is thrown for both syntax and resolution failures, so callers can catch one type.
+- Parse the whole pointer (validating every token's escapes) before walking the document, so syntax errors are reported even when resolution would fail earlier.
+- Own-property lookup via `Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call`, to avoid prototype pollution-style surprises.
+- Array tokens validated with `/^(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$/`.
+- Assumption: the document is JSON-compatible data; no validation of it is performed.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Tests run under `node --test`; since there is no build step, check how TypeScript is executed in the environment during apply.
