+## Why
+
+Our services need one standard way to refer to a value inside a JSON document. RFC 6901 (JSON Pointer) is that standard, and later features of this library will build on it.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returning the value a JSON Pointer refers to.
+- It throws when the pointer is not syntactically valid per RFC 6901, or when it does not resolve to a value of the document.
+- Out of scope: the URI fragment representation (`#/a/b`), and any write/update operation.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-pointer`: evaluating RFC 6901 JSON Pointers against a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New `src/` module and its tests; the package gains its first public export. No dependencies added.
